```tsx
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import { ThemeProvider, Container, Flex, Text, Icon, Button, TabProvider, TabList, Tab, TabPanel, Box } from '@gravity-ui/uikit';
import { House, CircleInfo, Gear, Sun, Moon } from '@gravity-ui/icons';

import { HomePage } from './pages/HomePage';
import { AboutPage } from './pages/AboutPage';
import { SettingsPage } from './pages/SettingsPage';

type Page = 'home' | 'about' | 'settings';
type ThemeName = 'light' | 'dark';

const THEME_STORAGE_KEY = 'app-theme';

function getInitialTheme(): ThemeName {
  const stored = localStorage.getItem(THEME_STORAGE_KEY);
  if (stored === 'light' || stored === 'dark') return stored;
  return window.matchMedia?.('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
}

export function App() {
  const [theme, setTheme] = useState<ThemeName>(getInitialTheme);
  const [page, setPage] = useState<Page>('home');

  useEffect(() => {
    localStorage.setItem(THEME_STORAGE_KEY, theme);
  }, [theme]);

  const toggleTheme = () => setTheme((t) => (t === 'light' ? 'dark' : 'light'));

  return (
    <ThemeProvider theme={theme}>
      <Flex direction="column" style={{ minHeight: '100vh' }}>
        <header ...>
          <Container maxWidth="l">
            <Flex alignItems="center" justifyContent="space-between" ...>
              <Text variant="header-1">Моё приложение</Text>
              <TabList value={page} onUpdate={(v) => setPage(v as Page)}>...
```

Hmm — can TabList be used standalone without TabProvider? TabProvider provides context; TabList may work with its own value/onUpdate props. The types show TabListProps has value/onUpdate optional. TabList probably works standalone if given value/onUpdate. But to be safe use TabProvider wrapping both TabList (in header) and TabPanel (content). TabProvider is just a context provider, so wrap whole app content in it.

Structure:

```tsx
<ThemeProvider theme={theme}>
  <TabProvider value={page} onUpdate={(v) => setPage(v as Page)}>
    <Flex direction="column" style={{minHeight: '100vh'}}>
      <Box as="header" spacing={{p: 4}} style={{borderBottom: '1px solid var(--g-color-line-generic)'}}>
        <Container maxWidth="l">
          <Flex alignItems="center" justifyContent="space-between" gap={4}>
            <Text variant="header-1">Gravity Demo</Text>
            <TabList size="l">
              <Tab value="home" icon={<Icon data={House} size={18} />}>Главная</Tab>
              <Tab value="about" icon={...}>О проекте</Tab>
              <Tab value="settings" icon={...}>Настройки</Tab>
            </TabList>
            <Button view="outlined" onClick={toggleTheme}>
              <Icon data={theme === 'light' ? Moon : Sun} size={16} />
              {theme === 'light' ? 'Тёмная' : 'Светлая'}
            </Button>
          </Flex>
        </Container>
      </Box>
      <Box as="main" spacing={{py: 6}} style={{flex: 1, minHeight: 0}}>
        <Container maxWidth="l">
          <TabPanel value="home"><HomePage onNavigate={setPage} /></TabPanel>
          <TabPanel value="about"><AboutPage /></TabPanel>
          <TabPanel value="settings"><SettingsPage theme={theme} onToggleTheme={toggleTheme} /></TabPanel>
        </Container>
      </Box>
    </Flex>
  </TabProvider>
</ThemeProvider>
```

Wait — Tab value prop: TabProps requires `value: string`. Good. Tab children as label.

Does TabList in a header work fine — sure.

Check Container props: maxWidth values? Check Container.d.ts quickly. And Flex props (direction, justifyContent names). Let me verify.

Pages:

HomePage: display text hero, three Cards (Rocket, Star, Thunderbolt), Button view="action" navigating to about.
AboutPage: Text header-1, Card with body text about Gravity UI.
SettingsPage: Card rows: Switch "Тёмная тема" checked={theme==='dark'} onUpdate={toggle}; maybe also show current theme Text.

Verify Container and Flex props.

